---
id: org.dxos.feed
name: Feed
version: 0.1.0
---

`@dxos/feed` is the feed store: the SQLite tables that hold every feed's blocks, on a device
(`EchoHost`) and on EDGE (the `FeedSpace` Durable Object in EDGE's db-service). This
spec covers the store's side of a feed's **indexing and retention options**: how it keeps them and
how it enforces retention.

The options are fields of the `Feed` ECHO object (`org.dxos.echo` [F-7]). The
store never reads that object; the indexer carries them down as a feed-options intent and calls
`setFeedOptions` (`org.dxos.index-core` [F-2]). What the indexer does with a
feed whose indexing is disabled is in that spec too [F-3].

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`     |
| `scenario` | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0` |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |
| `service`  | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`  |
| `table`    | `org.dxos.mdl.table@1.0`    |

## Concepts

```mdl
service FeedStore
  desc: |
    The feed store over one SQLite database. Every op is an
    Effect that requires SqlClient. EchoHost owns one per device; on EDGE each FeedSpace DO owns one per space.
    Only the ops this spec touches are listed; `# new` marks the ones it adds.
  ops:
    append(request: AppendRequest) → AppendResult                # sync push/pull; trims after insert [F-2.1, F-2.4]
    appendLocal(messages: LocalMessage[]) → Block[]              # local writes; trims after insert [F-2.1]
    query(request: QueryRequest) → QueryResponse                 # hides blocks past maxAge [F-2.2]
    subscribe(request: SubscribeRequest) → Stream<Block>         # hides blocks past maxAge [F-2.2]
    countBlocks(feed: FeedKey) → number
    deleteOldestBlocks(feed: FeedKey, count: number) → number
    setFeedOptions(feed: FeedKey, options: FeedOptions) → void   # new; stores and trims [F-1.1, F-1.2]
    getFeedOptions(feed: FeedKey) → FeedOptions | undefined      # new [F-1.1]
    trim(feed: FeedKey, now: Timestamp) → TrimResult             # new; both limits, at most TRIM_LIMIT blocks per call [F-2.3, F-2.7]
    trimAll(spaceId: SpaceId, now: Timestamp) → TrimResult       # new; every feed of a space, at open and on alarm, same bound [F-2.2, F-2.7]
  note: |
    FeedKey is { spaceId, feedNamespace, feedId }. TrimResult is { deleted: number; more: boolean }. FeedOptions is { indexing?: IndexingOptions; retention?:
    RetentionOptions } from the @dxos/echo Feed module (`org.dxos.echo` [F-7]).
```

```mdl
table feeds: One feed of a space, in one namespace.
  store: feed store (feed_migrations)
  columns:
    feedPrivateId: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT  # local row id; blocks reference it
    spaceId: TEXT
    feedId: TEXT                                      # the Feed object's entity id
    feedNamespace?: TEXT                              # data | trace
    options?: TEXT                                    # json FeedOptions; NULL = defaults [F-1.3]
  key: feedPrivateId
  unique:
    - (spaceId, feedId)
  new: options
```

```mdl
table blocks: One block (item) of a feed, in append order.
  store: feed store (feed_migrations)
  columns:
    insertionId: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT    # local append order
    feedPrivateId: INTEGER REFERENCES feeds(feedPrivateId)
    position?: INTEGER                                # assigned by the position authority; NULL until acknowledged
    sequence: INTEGER
    actorId: TEXT
    prevSequence?: INTEGER
    prevActorId?: TEXT
    timestamp: INTEGER                                # append time, ms since epoch; maxAge is measured from it
    data: BLOB
    encryptionKeyId?: TEXT
    iv?: BLOB
  key: insertionId
  unique:
    - (feedPrivateId, position)
  indexes:
    - idx_blocks_feedPrivateId_timestamp(feedPrivateId, timestamp): trim and hide by maxAge without a scan [F-2.2]
  new: idx_blocks_feedPrivateId_timestamp
```

```mdl
table trimmed_blocks: One block deleted by retention whose index rows are not removed yet.
  store: feed store (feed_migrations)
  columns:
    id: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT   # monotonic; clearTrimmed is bounded by it
    feedPrivateId: INTEGER
    insertionId: INTEGER
    position?: INTEGER
  key: id
  new: table
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Options in the feed store

  req F-1.1:
    when: FeedStore.setFeedOptions({ spaceId, feedId, namespace, indexing, retention }) is called
    then: the options are stored in table:feeds.options (a new migration adds the column), creating
          the row when the feed has no blocks yet, and getFeedOptions returns them

  req F-1.2:
    when: setFeedOptions is called with the options already stored
    then: it changes nothing and trims nothing

  req F-1.3:
    when: a feed has no stored options
    then: indexing is enabled and only the host's own limits apply (see [F-2.6])

  req F-1.4:
    when: feeds sync between a device and EDGE
    then: options are not part of the sync protocol; each store learns them only from its own
          index pass of the Feed object

  req F-1.5:
    when: FeedSpace (EDGE) receives setFeedOptions from the Indexer DO
    then: it is a public RPC method listed in the DO's rpcMethods and applies the options to the
          space's FeedStore in one transaction
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Retention

  req F-2.1:
    when: a feed has retention.maxLength = N
    then: after every append, every sync pull and every options apply, the store keeps at most the
          N newest blocks of the feed and deletes the rest in the same transaction

  req F-2.2:
    when: a feed has retention.maxAge = D
    then: query and subscribe never return a block whose timestamp is older than now - D, from the
          moment it expires; the store deletes such blocks at the next append, pull, options apply,
          store open, or (on EDGE) Durable Object alarm; the position authority keeps a feed's
          highest-positioned block (hidden from reads) until a newer one exists

  req F-2.3:
    when: both limits are set
    then: a block is dropped when it breaks either limit

  req F-2.4:
    when: a sync pull brings in blocks that the local retention would drop
    then: they are dropped in the same transaction that inserts them, and the pull does not request
          them again

  req F-2.5:
    when: retention would delete a block that holds the newest version of a live feed object
    then: the block is still deleted; retention trims in insertion order and does not compact superseded
          versions (compacting superseded versions of live feed objects is separate work)

  req F-2.6:
    when: a trace-namespace feed on EDGE has stored options
    then: the limit is the smaller of retention.maxLength and config.queues.maxTraceQueueItems;
          with no maxLength, maxTraceQueueItems applies as it does today

  req F-2.9:
    when: a replica store (one that does not assign positions) trims
    then: it never deletes a block that has no position yet, so a local write is never lost
          before it is pushed

  req F-2.10:
    when: trim deletes blocks
    then: it logs each one in table:trimmed_blocks in the same transaction, so the indexer can
          remove their rows durably; a sync pull whose cursor block was trimmed does not treat
          the empty slot as a server rewind

  req F-2.7:
    when: trim or trimAll runs
    then: it deletes at most TRIM_LIMIT blocks (10,000) in one transaction, in insertion order (blocks.insertionId) oldest first, and returns
          more = true when blocks past a limit remain; the host calls it again until more is false —
          EchoHost at once, EDGE from the FeedSpace alarm — so one call never exceeds a Durable
          Object's CPU or storage-transaction limits

  req F-2.8:
    when: trim runs again with the same options and clock, or runs concurrently with another trim
    then: it deletes nothing further than the limits require; repeated and interrupted calls converge
          on the same retained blocks
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Retention by length
  given: a feed with 10 items and retention { maxLength: 5 }, applied
  when: 3 more items are appended
  then:
    - Feed.query(feed) returns the 5 newest items
    - countBlocks for the feed is 5
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Retention by age
  given: a feed with retention { maxAge: 1 hour } and items appended 2 hours and 10 minutes ago
  when: Feed.query(feed) runs, before any trim
  then:
    - only the item from 10 minutes ago is returned
    - after the next append the 2-hour-old block is gone from the store
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: EDGE applies the same options
  given: a feed with retention { maxLength: 2 } replicated to EDGE
  when: EDGE's Indexer DO applies the feed's options intent
  then:
    - FeedSpace.setFeedOptions stores the options and the EDGE store keeps 2 blocks
    - a device that pulls the feed from EDGE stores at most 2 blocks
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Retention is a maximum length and/or a maximum age.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Indexing and retention options set on the Feed ECHO object flow down to the feed in the feed store.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Options live on the feeds row of each store and are not part of feed sync. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.4]
  why: The Feed object already replicates; a second path for the same value could disagree with it.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Retention trims on append, pull, options apply and store open; expired items are hidden from reads at once and deleted lazily. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.4]
  why: Age expires with no write to trigger a trim, so reads must filter; deleting lazily keeps the cost on paths that already write.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: On EDGE, the trace-feed limit maxTraceQueueItems stays a cap; a feed's maxLength can lower it, not raise it. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.6]
  why: The config value bounds EDGE storage cost, which a space member must not be able to lift by editing an object.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The options are one nullable JSON column, `feeds.options`, where NULL means the defaults. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [feeds, F-1.1, F-1.3]
  why: The store reads the options as one value on every trim; JSON keeps a later option from needing another migration, and NULL keeps existing rows valid with no backfill.
  rejected:
    - "One column per option (maxLength, maxAge, indexingEnabled): every new option is an ALTER, and the store never queries by them."
```

```mdl
decision D-7: FeedStore gains setFeedOptions, getFeedOptions, trim and trimAll; retention runs through trim, which deleteOldestBlocks and a new timestamp index serve. Fills in [D-1] and [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FeedStore, blocks, F-2.2, F-2.3]
  why: One trim op keeps both limits in one place for append, pull, apply, open and alarm; without an index on (feedPrivateId, timestamp), age trimming scans the feed.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Trim has a high upper limit per call, so it does not break Cloudflare, and stays idempotent.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FeedStore, F-2.7, F-2.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The limit is 10,000 blocks per call, deleted oldest first in one transaction; trim reports `more`, and the host repeats it (EchoHost at once, EDGE from the FeedSpace alarm). Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [FeedStore, F-2.7]
  why: Deleting oldest first keeps every partial trim a valid prefix of the full one, which is what makes repeating it idempotent; 10,000 small rows is well inside one Durable Object request, and a first trim after enabling retention on a large feed can otherwise delete millions.
  rejected:
    - "Delete everything in one call: unbounded CPU and transaction size on a large feed."
```

```mdl
decision D-10: "Oldest" means lowest blocks.insertionId — local insertion order — for maxLength trimming, not the position the authority assigned. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.5, F-2.7]
  why: A block has no position until the authority acknowledges it, so position cannot order every block; insertionId always exists and is what deleteOldestBlocks already uses. The two orders can differ on a replica, which the review of this spec flagged.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: A replica never trims a block with no position, and the position authority keeps its highest-positioned block until a newer one exists. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.2, F-2.9]
  why: An unpushed block exists nowhere else; and the authority assigns the next position as max + 1, so deleting the top block would reissue positions that replicas already hold, which they read as a rollback.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Trimmed blocks are logged in a `trimmed_blocks` table in the trim transaction, and the sync client treats an empty slot at its cursor as trimmed rather than as a rewind. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.10, trimmed_blocks]
  why: The log makes removing trimmed items from the index crash-safe; without the sync change, a replica whose cursor block was trimmed re-pulled the whole namespace on every sync.
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext service
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0
  desc: An external or system-level dependency providing named operations.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    loading?: eager | lazy
    ops?: OpMap                 # name(params) → ReturnType
    errors?: ErrorMap
    note?: Prose
```

```mdl
ext table
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.table@1.0
  desc: |
    A SQL table a component owns. The identifier is the table name; the inline prose is what one row
    is. Columns, keys and indexes are the schema after the spec's changes.
  fields:
    store: Prose                # the database, and its migration-history table in parentheses
    columns: FieldMap           # `name[?]: SQLTYPE [constraint …]  # meaning`; `?` allows NULL
    key?: Prose                 # the primary key, as a column list
    unique?: ProseList          # other unique keys, as column lists
    indexes?: ProseList         # `name(columns): why a query needs it`
    new?: Prose                 # `table`, or the columns this spec adds
  inline-prose: true
  syntax: |
    table feeds: One feed of a space, by namespace.
      store: feed store (feed_migrations)
      columns:
        feedPrivateId: INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT  # local row id; blocks reference it
        spaceId: TEXT
        feedId: TEXT                                      # the Feed object's entity id
        options?: TEXT                                    # json FeedOptions; NULL = defaults
      key: feedPrivateId
      new: options
```
